\begin{abstract}
AstroField-Sim and its hardware counterpart FINS-ADPE constitute the first 
encrypted, continuous, relativistic astrophysical simulation engine capable of 
executing Vlasov-Poisson, magnetohydrodynamic (MHD), and post-Newtonian (1PN) 
field evolution over homomorphically encrypted sky survey datasets. The system 
integrates Field-Induced Transformer Nodes (FITN), FI-HVE lattice encryption, 
Chebyshev-expanded Poisson solvers, and a million-node tensor lattice accelerated 
by cryo-cooled multi-FPGA and GPU silicon. This paper presents the full 
mathematical formulation, stability analysis, hardware validation, and 
scientific benchmark results demonstrating unprecedented numerical robustness, 
cryptographic integrity, and relativistic accuracy.
\end{abstract}

