\section{FI-HVE Encryption Model}
Astrophysical vectors $m \in \mathbb{R}^d$ are encoded into ring-LWE ciphertexts:
\begin{equation}
    \mathbf{c} = (\mathbf{a}, \mathbf{b} = \mathbf{a}\mathbf{s} + \Delta m + e),
\end{equation}
where $\mathbf{s}$ is the secret key, $e$ is Gaussian noise, and $\Delta$ is a 
scaling factor. All gravitational and MHD operators are computed homomorphically.

\section{Field-Induced Transformer Nodes (FITN)}
FITN redefines attention as a physics-biased operator:
\begin{equation}
    A_{ij} = \mathrm{Softmax}\left(
        \frac{Q_i K_j^T}{\sqrt{d}} + \Phi_{ij}
    \right),
\end{equation}
where $\Phi_{ij}$ is the encrypted gravitational or MHD potential:
\begin{equation}
    \Phi_{ij} = -\alpha \norm{\mathbf{x}_i - \mathbf{x}_j}^2.
\end{equation}

Node evolution follows:
\begin{equation}
    \frac{d h_i}{dt} = \mathcal{F}(h_i, \Phi) - 
    \lambda \mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{PDE}}.
\end{equation}

