\section{1PN Relativistic Corrections}
The scalar potential obeys:
\begin{equation}
\nabla^2 \Phi =
4\pi G\rho +
\frac{1}{c^2}
\left(
3\ddot{\Phi} +
4\pi G\rho v^2 +
12\pi G P -
2\Phi\nabla^2\Phi
\right),
\end{equation}
and the vector potential satisfies:
\begin{equation}
\nabla^2 \mathbf{w} = 4\pi G\rho\mathbf{v}.
\end{equation}

The relativistic Vlasov equation:
\begin{equation}
\frac{\partial f}{\partial t}
+
\frac{\mathbf{p}}{\gamma m}\cdot\nabla_{\mathbf{x}}f
+
\mathbf{F}_{\mathrm{1PN}}\cdot\nabla_{\mathbf{p}}f
=0.
\end{equation}

